        "comments": "The assembly fSarPil1.1 is based on 33x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using rapid curation. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. There are large haplotype inversions on the following chromosomes: Chromosome 5 from\n4.03-31.1Mb, Chromosome 8 from\n6.87-30.93Mb, Chromosome 9 from\n4.98-33.85Mb, Chromosome 15 from\n3.26-29.76, Chromosome 17 - a double inversion from\n17.96-30.93. ALT assembly has been assembled into chromosomes as a merged assembly of both haplotypes was used for curation.",
